---
import LandingHeader from "../../components/LandingHeader.astro";
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const repositoryUrl = "https://github.com/nabilrn/MyPaas";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | MyPaaS"
  description="How the MyPaaS public website and self-hosted MyPaaS instances handle browser preferences, operational data, and connected services."
  path="/privacy/"
>
  <LandingHeader />
  <main class="policy-page">
    <article class="policy-shell">
      <header>
        <p>Policy</p>
        <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
        <div>
          This policy separates the public MyPaaS website from the MyPaaS software
          that an operator installs on their own infrastructure.
        </div>
        <span>Effective 16 August 2026</span>
      </header>

      <section>
        <h2>1. Public website</h2>
        <p>
          The public website is a static informational site. As shipped, it does not
          provide accounts, advertising, behavioral analytics, or tracking cookies.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>The theme preference may be stored locally in your browser under <code>mypaas-theme</code>.</li>
          <li>The cookie preference control stores your Accept or Reject choice locally under <code>mypaas-cookie-consent</code>.</li>
          <li>The current build does not load analytics or advertising cookies regardless of that preference.</li>
          <li>The installation copy button writes the displayed command to your clipboard only after you click it.</li>
          <li>The hosting or network provider may process standard request metadata such as IP address, user agent, requested path, and timestamp for delivery and security.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>2. Cookie and browser-storage choices</h2>
        <p>
          The site exposes explicit Accept and Reject controls for optional cookies. The choice is stored locally so the notice does not need to appear on every visit.
          The current public build does not attach optional analytics or advertising scripts to either choice.
        </p>
        <p>
          Necessary browser storage used for interface preferences is separate from optional tracking. Clearing site data in your browser resets these saved preferences.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>3. Self-hosted MyPaaS instances</h2>
        <p>
          A MyPaaS instance is operated by the person or organization that installs it.
          That operator controls the server, database, domain, authorized users, backups,
          retention, and connected third-party services.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you use someone else's instance, contact that instance operator about access,
          correction, export, retention, or deletion of your data.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>4. Data an instance may process</h2>
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Category</th><th>Examples and purpose</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><strong>Identity</strong></td><td>GitHub identity data used for OAuth authentication and instance authorization.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Repository configuration</strong></td><td>Repository URL, selected branch, deployment model, ports, environment configuration, and webhook settings used to deploy a project.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Project environment</strong></td><td>Environment keys and values used at runtime. Persisted project environment values are encrypted before storage.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Operational records</strong></td><td>Deployment history, commit identifiers, build output, runtime logs, status, metrics, and failure context.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Audit records</strong></td><td>Authenticated administration and project actions used for troubleshooting and accountability.</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>5. Connected services</h2>
        <p>Depending on the operator's configuration, a MyPaaS instance can interact with:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>GitHub</strong> for OAuth, repository access, and signed webhook events.</li>
          <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> for Tunnel ingress, TLS termination, and related edge processing.</li>
          <li><strong>Git hosts and public OCI registries</strong> selected by the operator or project configuration.</li>
          <li><strong>Operator-controlled backup destinations</strong> used for recovery outside the local VM failure domain.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Those providers process data under their own terms and privacy policies.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>6. Storage, retention, and deletion</h2>
        <p>
          Instance data is stored on infrastructure controlled by the operator. Retention depends on instance configuration,
          deployment history cleanup, project deletion, scheduled backups, and any off-host recovery policy maintained by the operator.
        </p>
        <p>
          Copies can remain in operator-managed backups until those backups expire. Engine-managed storage can also require
          explicit handling during VM migration according to the documented migration boundary.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>7. Security and responsibility</h2>
        <p>
          MyPaaS includes access controls, encrypted project environment storage, signed webhook verification,
          explicit routing boundaries, DB Studio write-session controls, and audit records. The API retains privileged
          container-engine authority, so the current single-host architecture is not a hostile multi-tenant security boundary.
        </p>
        <p>
          The operator remains responsible for host security, SSH access, credential rotation, backup verification,
          repository review, capacity planning, and incident response.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>8. Questions and changes</h2>
        <p>
          For an installed instance, contact its operator first. For questions about the open-source project or this public policy,
          use the contact method published in the <a href={repositoryUrl} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MyPaaS repository</a>.
          Do not post credentials, environment values, migration URLs, or private logs in a public issue.
        </p>
        <p>
          This policy may change when the public website or MyPaaS data model changes. The effective date above identifies the current version.
        </p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
.policy-page{min-height:calc(100vh - 4.5rem);padding:clamp(3.5rem,7vw,6.5rem) 0;border-top:1px solid var(--app-border);background:var(--app-bg)}.policy-shell{width:min(calc(100% - 2.5rem),54rem);margin-inline:auto}header{padding-bottom:2.5rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--app-border-strong)}header>p{margin:0 0 .8rem;color:var(--app-accent-strong);font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:.64rem;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase}h1{margin:0;font-size:clamp(3rem,6vw,5.4rem);font-weight:590;letter-spacing:-.058em;line-height:.98}header>div{max-width:42rem;margin-top:1.2rem;color:var(--app-muted);font-size:1rem;line-height:1.7}header>span{display:block;margin-top:1.1rem;color:var(--app-subtle);font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:.68rem}section{padding-top:3rem}h2{margin:0 0 1rem;font-size:clamp(1.55rem,3vw,2.25rem);font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.036em}p,li,td{color:var(--app-muted);font-size:.87rem;line-height:1.75}p{margin:0 0 1rem}ul{margin:.8rem 0 1rem;padding-left:1.25rem}li+li{margin-top:.45rem}strong{color:var(--app-ink);font-weight:620}code{padding:.12rem .3rem;border:1px solid var(--app-border);border-radius:.25rem;background:var(--app-surface-muted);color:var(--app-ink);font-size:.78em}a{color:var(--app-accent-strong);text-underline-offset:.2em}table{width:100%;margin:1.25rem 0;border-collapse:collapse}th,td{padding:.8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--app-border);text-align:left;vertical-align:top}th{border-bottom-color:var(--app-border-strong);color:var(--app-subtle);font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:.62rem;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase}
@media(max-width:600px){.policy-shell{width:min(calc(100% - 1.25rem),54rem)}table{display:block;overflow-x:auto}}
</style>
